  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Afghanistan Crisis Appeal</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The DEC has launched an urgent appeal to help save lives as the humanitarian crisis intensifies in Afghanistan, where eight million people are on the brink of starvation. Appeals are being broadcast on 15 December 2021 to national audiences after the news on BBC TV and radio channels, ITV, Channel 4, Channel 5 and Sky.

Conflict and&#x202f;economic collapse,&#x202f;coupled with&#x202f;the&#x202f;worst drought in 27 years&#x202f;and the Covid-19 pandemic,&#x202f;have brought&#x202f;Afghanistan&#x202f;to&#x202f;a tipping&#x202f;point. 22 million face acute hunger and one million children are at risk of dying in the next three months. Lives are already being lost. 

The DEC brings together 15 leading UK aid charities to call on the British public to help people in times of crisis overseas.</narrative>
  </description>
